bats, when killed, should on occasion leave one or two wings of bat.
a wing of bat is sort of a mini-boomerang with shuriken-like accuracy
and damage. it if misses and is unimpeded it returns to you. whether it
hits you or you catch it depends on your throwing skill.        @-->--
like daggers, wings of bat survive their attack and tend to    ^      v
travel in a tight counter-clockwise loop (ex. thrown left).     --<---
wings of bat could be dipped in any potion and would carry the effect of
the last dipped potion, if possible.

newts, when killed, should on occasion leave an "eye of newt", a food
item of little nutrition. eating an eye of newt would temporarily give
you helm-of-telepathy-like telepathy (100-300 moves, you feel a
peculiar mental acuity, you feel your acuity passing).

lizards, when killed, should on occasion leave a lizard gizzard instead
of a corpse. a lizard gizzard is a tiny tool like a bag but only capable
of holding small items like an eye of newt or a wing of bat or a few rocks
or rings. any respectable shaman knows that the combination of a lizard
gizzard, eye of newt and wing of bat is powerful magic and would (randomly)
transform a ring or rock also contained therein (at least a few times
before disintegrating it).

in talking to a priest you might find that are you asked to forgo your
pagan ways if you're carrying the lizard gizzard containing eye of newt
and wing of bat. if you comply and give up the gizzard you might find
the priest generously offers to bless something in your inventory or
converts you to his alignment. who knows ...

